    "title": "See inside $15M Lake Norman estate, Charlotte area's most expensive listing - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Evan Moore ,\n7 hours ago\nA new Lake Norman estate has claimed the title of the Charlotte region’s most expensive home on the market – with a price tag of $15 million.\nLocated at 1890 Yacht Club Drive, in Denver , the property spans 2.8 acres and boasts more than 1,000 feet of shoreline. Marketed as the “crown jewel of Lake Norman,” the estate offers resort-style living with a main home, three attached townhomes and a sailing club featuring more than 120 boat slips.\nThe four-bedroom, three-and-a-half-bath main house features an open layout with a two-story stone fireplace, soaring wood ceilings and panoramic lake views. A rooftop terrace provides a full 360-degree view of the water, while the primary suite includes dual closets, a hidden safe room and a luxurious bath.\nThe additional townhomes add seven bedrooms and four baths, which is ideal for guests or multi-generational living. The sailing club includes a meeting room and two bedrooms, enhancing the property’s flexibility for entertaining or retreats, the listing says.\nHere’s a look inside:\nThe four-bedroom, three-and-a-half-bath main house features an open layout with a two-story stone fireplace, soaring wood ceilings and panoramic lake views. Courtesy of Canopy This spacious gourmet kitchen boasts extensive medium-toned wood cabinetry, wood floors, a large central island, a long breakfast bar with a light countertop and recessed lighting. Courtesy of Canopy The dining room provides an excellent view of the water. Courtesy of Canopy This distinctive bathroom showcases script-covered wallpaper, a warm wooden vanity with a white countertop and a brass-trimmed glass shower enclosure, all set on a dark wood-toned floor. Courtesy of Canopy Enjoy expansive outdoor living on this deep, covered wooden deck, which runs the length of the home and provides a spectacular, shaded panoramic view of Lake Norman. Courtesy of Canopy The property features more than 120 boat slips. Courtesy of Canopy For more information about the listing, contact LeeAnn Miller at leeann.miller@allentate.com.\n‘Stranger Things,’ safe spaces and sweet sips: Was this Charlotte cafe worth it?\nWho has the cutest dog, cat in Charlotte? Enter our contest for bragging rights",
